<title>USA: Electropharmacology to conduct new trials.</title>
<headline>Electropharmacology to conduct new trials.</headline>
<dateline>POMPANO BEACH, Fla. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elecropharmacology Inc said on Thursday it will conduct new clinical trials for its SoftPulse device, after deciding that results of a previous trial could not be substantiated.</p>
<p>The company is seeking pre-market approval for the device from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. The test concerned its effectiveness at reducing edema in Grade I and Grade II ankle sprains.</p>
